---
description: Shell blocks — balanced quotes; avoid PS2 hangs (dquote>, quote>, bquote>)
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
message: |
  ## Shell hygiene (QuoteGuard)

  **Default:** one logical command per line; no trailing `\`, `|`, `&&`, or unmatched `(` / `{` / `[` at EOL.

  **Quoting:** Even counts of `"` and `'` outside the other quote style; backticks and `$(` closed; prefer `printf '%s\n' 'literal'` over fragile `echo` for odd data.

  **Multi-line:** Prefer `cat <<'EOF' > file` with a **single-quoted** delimiter; close delimiter on its own line.

  **Fenced `bash` blocks:** ```bash … ``` only; no `$` prompts in copy-paste commands.

  **If you see `dquote>` / `quote>` / `bquote>` in output:** stop chaining; Ctrl-C; `stty sane; reset || true`; re-emit a single-line, balanced command.
